        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory): search by filenames and paths",
        "body": "Closes #94102\n\nMaintainer-owned replacement for #96052. This keeps @Pick-cat's implementation as the credited base while allowing the reviewed tree to use current `main` ancestry; the contributor fork's verified web-editor path could update its tree but could not rewrite its stale ancestry.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where memory search would miss relevant notes when users searched for a filename or path term that was absent from the note body.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIndexes normalized paths in a separate one-row-per-source FTS table, preserving the existing body index, BM25 scores, snippets, and embeddings. Exact full-path, basename, and stem matches receive deterministic precedence; partial Unicode path matches, multi-term fallback, source filters, atomic shadow-index publication, and temporal/MMR ranking retain their existing owner boundaries.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can find memories by full path, filename, stem, or partial Unicode path text without polluting body relevance. Existing content and semantic search behavior remains unchanged when paths do not match, and disabling FTS still removes all FTS-owned tables.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact replacement head: `daea62fb242784c5f73f53b8d9238ba57dab4a96`; GitHub-verified, based directly on `96f0983a85b5a7798d35e97d8f530fed9b567929`, and tree-identical to the reviewed local branch.\n- Fresh full-branch autoreview and independent full-surface audit: clean across bounded candidate partitions, Unicode/fallback ranking, temporal/MMR behavior, stable FTS row identity, shadow publication, and the atomic agent-database v1-to-v2 migration.\n- Regression coverage includes full path/basename/stem/partial matching, NFC/NFD and non-Latin text, exact/non-exact candidate caps, multi-term fallback, body/path score separation, temporal decay, MMR grouping, malformed-schema rollback, and concurrent owner/version claims.\n- Exact-head sanitized AWS/Linux proof: `run_297dcc97f02a` passed 237 focused SDK, schema, migration, ranking, and tool tests; hosted CI run `29161927119` completed with 72 pass, 27 intentional skips, and 0 failures.\n- Exact-head package proof: `run_2eda117a0eb1` built and validated the tarball, installed it into an isolated prefix, passed 8/8 JSON/human search assertions (including exact/partial Unicode and a negative control), and passed 2/2 rename/reindex assertions.\n",
